  "result": "The 3-field signup form won, and it's now live for 100% of users in Development. I committed the cleanup on branch `ship-three-field-signup` (no PR, since there's no remote) and archived the `signup_form` flag.\n\n- **Result:** The 3-field form converted at 25.1% (128 of 510) against 19.6% for the 6-field form (96 of 490). Flagsmith's probability that the 3-field form is better was 96.7%, and its verdict was `ship:three_field`.\n- **Weaker than you expected:** Both simulated rates came out lower than the 20% and 32% I fed in. The 95% interval on the lift is −1.9% to +58.1%, so it still includes zero. I shipped because Flagsmith's verdict said to and you'd approved shipping, but it isn't a decisive result.\n- **Code:** I removed the 6-field path and the flag check. The `signup_completed` tracking stays on the 3-field form. The simulation script is at `C:\\Users\\<user>\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\9d334f8170809723\\1e14ffb0-de7f-4325-ba38-e54a8d1c3f98\\scratchpad\\sim.js`.\n- **Rollback:** `bash scripts/rollback.sh signup_form .flagsmith-skill/rollback/signup_form-20261128T013631Z.state`, run from the skill's folder (`.claude/skills/flagsmith-experiment`).\n- **Audit log:** `.flagsmith-skill/audit.log`\n\nThe experiment is `1518`.",
